    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded an email-uniqueness rule to `POST /api/owners`, mirroring the existing telephone/household uniqueness checks:\n\n1. **`RequireUniqueEmail.java`** (function step) \u2014 after the email is normalized/lower-cased by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, it compares the request email against every existing owner's email (lower-cased, trimmed) via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`. Email is optional, so a null/blank email skips the check. On a match it throws `DuplicateEmailException`.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** \u2014 a checked escalation carrying the offending email.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** + **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with body `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`, consistent with the telephone/household handlers.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `requireUniqueEmail` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline between `requireUniqueHousehold` and `requireCityCapacity`, so the rejection happens before any owner is persisted.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and all other tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
